.TH ckman-oath-accounts-set-default 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-oath\-accounts\-set\-default \- Mark an existing HOTP account as the touch keyboard\-emulation default
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-oath\-accounts\-set\-default\fR [\fB\-\-slot\fR] [\fB\-\-enter\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-password\fR] [\fB\-\-remember\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIQUERY\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mark an existing HOTP account as the touch keyboard\-emulation default
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-slot\fR \fI<SLOT>\fR [default: short]
Touch slot (firmware 3.0+ for long)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
short
.IP \(bu 2
long
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-enter\fR
Append a Return keystroke after the emitted code (firmware 3.0+)
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fI<PASSWORD>\fR
The password to unlock the OATH application
.TP
\fB\-\-remember\fR
Remember the password on this machine (long\-only: the global \-r/\-\-reader owns the short flag)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIQUERY\fR>
A query to match a single account (as shown in "list")
